message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper below."
title: "HALT: Certifying Trust Horizons in Action-Conditioned Robotic World Models"
abstract: >-
  Model-based robot controllers treat the imagination horizon as a fixed
  hyperparameter, yet the number of steps for which a world model remains
  dynamically valid is state-, action- and context-dependent. HALT
  (Horizon-Adaptive Latent Trust) is a wrapper that converts a world model into
  one that reports a certified, state-dependent trust horizon with a
  distribution-free guarantee, by coupling a monotone quantile head over
  deployment-available features with simultaneous split-conformal calibration.
type: conference-paper
